# Accepted vulnerabilities, each with a reason and a review date.
#
# An entry here suppresses a FIXABLE finding, which means it is a deliberate
# decision to ship known risk. Every one needs all three lines. An entry with
# no expiry is a hole nobody revisits, so `exp:` is mandatory — Trivy drops
# the suppression once that date passes, and the build fails again until
# somebody looks.

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# torch 2.5.1 → 2.6.0 (ai-service)
#
# CVE-2025-32434 is a deserialization flaw in `torch.load`. This service never
# calls it on untrusted input: the only weights it loads come from the
# sentence-transformers model it downloads at boot from a pinned repository,
# and no user-supplied file reaches torch at any point — uploads are parsed by
# pdfminer/pypdf/python-docx and only ever become text before embedding.
#
# The fix is a MINOR version bump of the inference engine underneath both the
# bi-encoder and the cross-encoder. That changes model numerics and is not
# something to do inside a containerization change without re-running the
# retrieval quality checks. Scheduled deliberately, not skipped.
#
# Review: bump to 2.6.0 and re-run the ai-service retrieval suite.
CVE-2025-32434 exp:2026-11-30
